# Architecture

Build the application as a **modular, reusable system**. Pair with [child-experience.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/child-experience.mdc) for play UX, [child-ui-components.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/child-ui-components.mdc) for child-facing UI implementation, [little-adventure-character.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/little-adventure-character.mdc) for the canonical character, and [little-adventure-world.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/little-adventure-world.mdc) for environment/props design boundaries.

## Page and component boundaries

- Do **not** place large amounts of application logic inside page components. Pages orchestrate layout, routing, and wiring — not domain rules or activity mechanics.
- Prefer **small reusable components** with a single clear responsibility.
- Keep a **clear separation between UI and business logic** (hooks, services, pure functions, or modules — follow whatever pattern the repo already uses).
- Use **typed data structures** for content, session state, and challenge payloads so activities stay predictable and safe to extend.

## Data-driven learning content

- **Do not hardcode** individual learning content directly into components. Words, numbers, days, and future learning material belong in **data or configuration** (JSON, CMS-shaped types, seed files, etc.), not scattered through the UI.
- UI should **render from props or loaded config**, not embed lesson-specific literals except for dev fixtures isolated from production paths.

## Challenge types and session engine

- Learning activities must be implemented as **reusable challenge types** (one implementation per interaction pattern, many content instances).
- Design so **new challenge types can be added without rewriting the session engine**. The engine advances sessions, selects challenges, and delegates rendering/scoring to typed challenge handlers or registries.
- **Reusable interaction patterns** (tap-to-choose, drag-to-match, etc.) should be shared across activities; see [sensory-friendly-interaction.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/sensory-friendly-interaction.mdc) for consistent feedback.

## Abstraction discipline

- **Avoid premature abstraction.** Introduce shared modules, base components, or generic engines only when reuse is **clear** (second real use case, or a stable contract the product already depends on).
- When abstracting, prefer **narrow interfaces** (challenge type + content schema) over large “god” frameworks.
- Do **not** introduce a generic game engine or heavy visual framework unless explicitly requested.

## Separation of concerns

Keep these boundaries explicit in design and implementation:

- **Learning / game logic** — challenge rules, correctness, session engine
- **Character implementation** — canonical `LittleAdventureCharacter` shell and figure (see [little-adventure-character.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/little-adventure-character.mdc))
- **Visual assets** — character production art, optional **illustrated environment** art, and props consumed by UI; no ad-hoc per-game character art; environment assets must not embed character or application UI
- **World / scene composition** — layered environment (illustration asset and/or simple markup), character, optional interaction props, then existing learning UI per [little-adventure-world.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/little-adventure-world.mdc); presentational, composed by screens/views; must not become a generic scene engine or duplicate challenge/progression logic
- **Audio** — centralized semantic playback ([little-adventure-audio.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/little-adventure-audio.mdc))
- **Celebration / progression** — success flow, Good Job, Next, child-guided continue ([little-adventure-celebration-progression.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/little-adventure-celebration-progression.mdc))
- **Screen / layout composition** — pages and views orchestrate wiring; they do not duplicate domain rules inside presentational children

Presentational components (including the character) receive props and render; they do not own challenge or progression state.

## Practical checklist

- New activity: add **content/config** + **challenge type** (or reuse existing type); page stays thin.
- New interaction pattern: new challenge type + register with session engine; do not fork one-off page logic.
- Business rules (correctness, progression, scoring if any) live **outside** presentational components.
- New illustrated scene: follow `docs/design/` artwork specs when present; compose **environment asset + `LittleAdventureCharacter` + existing UI** without a scene engine; verify **rendered visual coherence** on tablet for major child-facing visual work.
